{"body":"# Verify OTP or biometric for ABHA address login

## In plain words

Completes the [ABHA address](/docs/hiecm/v3/getting-started/glossary#abha-address) login. Send the same `scope` as the request call and the `txnId`, with the encrypted [OTP](/docs/hiecm/v3/getting-started/glossary#otp) or, for fingerprint, the capture in `fingerPrintAuthPid`. The response lists the person's ABHA addresses in `users` and carries `tokens.token`. Send that token as the `X-token` header to the profile, PHR card and QR code calls.

## How you know it worked

A 200 with `authResult` `success`. A 200 can also report an expired OTP, so read `authResult` and not the status alone.

## When it goes wrong

A 400 with `ABDM-9999` names the refused part in its message, such as an invalid scope or transaction id. Request a new OTP when the `txnId` is refused.","catalogue_version":"2026.09.16","doc_url":"/docs/hiecm/v3/api/m1/endpoints/m1-abha-address-login-mobile-otp/03-m1-post-v3-phr-web-login-abha-verify-mobile-otp#m1-phr-verify","gateway":"hiecm","id":"hiecm.endpoint.m1-phr-verify","milestone":"M1","operation":"m1_post_v3_phr_web_login_abha_verify_mobile_otp","summary":"Completes an ABHA address login and returns the X-token for the profile, card and QR calls.","title":"Verify OTP or biometric for ABHA address login","type":"endpoint"}
